			<tr valign="top">
				<td id="mainbody">
				
				<table cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" border="0">
					<tr>
						<td><p class="bodycopy"><span class="subhead1">Partnering<br></span>
						One key contributor to the success of our projects is our strong focus on partnering with our clients. We make the effort to understand your business, while recognizing that no one knows your business better than you do. Our experience has shown us that customer involvement is one of the critical factors in increasing quality and implementing the appropriate solution. Our approach bridges the communication gap that often exists between consultant and client on a project. As a true partner, we share the risk that is often encountered in mission critical projects by committing to do whatever it takes to make your project a success.</p>
						
						<p class="bodycopy"><span class="subhead1">Knowledge Transfer<br></span>
						A common goal for all our engagements, regardless of the project scope, is to leave our clients with increased knowledge, skills and autonomy. This transition to independence is a continual process that occurs throughout the project and provides much more than just training at the close of an engagement. Knowledge transfer is a critical component in creating quality, sustaining solutions for our clients.</p>
						
						<p class="bodycopy"><span class="subhead1">Methodology<br></span>
						We believe that methodologies exist to give you a framework to guide you through a process while ensuring a consistent approach to the solution. Defining the business processes, understanding the enterprise architecture requirements and developing solid applications should all be approached from a consistent, yet flexible framework. Enterprise Framework&#153; is our solution.</p>
						
						<p class="bodycopy"><span class="subhead1">Project Management<br></span>
						Our approach to project management goes hand in hand with the framework that we use for all our engagements. Risk management, project planning, issues resolution, team communication and estimating skills are all fundamental to effective project management. We have developed expert tools for issue tracking and resolution to facilitate our project management functions. The true test of successful project management is when the project comes in on time and on budget, the deliverables meet your expectations, and most of all, your vision is realized.</p></td>
					</tr>
				</table>
				
